The dumplogs are more accurate in this regard, of course.  Anecdotal
opinion, I rate the amulets in this order for "regular wear", assuming
vanilla NH:

poison resistance (unless I have PR already)
reflection (unless I have another source)
ESP (unless I have blindfoldless ESP somehow)
life saving
magical breathing
unchanging

By "regular wear", I mean the amulet you put on and forget about until
you see one that's higher up your list.  The bottom two I'll keep 
for special occasions, but will only wear all the time if I don't have
one of the first four.

Poison resistance is an odd case, as most characters rush for PR early
in the game to avoid instadeaths.  It rates higher than anything else
until you actually get PR (in the early game, poison is more common than
reflectable wand/ray attacks), at which point it becomes polyfodder.

I prefer to wear SDSM or carry a shield than burn my amulet slot on
reflection, as ESP and life-saving are more slot-restricted.  I rate ESP
above life-saving because when i last played, I was in the habit of
playing around the opportunity for careless mistakes, and the
information gained via ESP was more useful throughout the game.  

Put otherwise: If you're in the habit of dying, one AoLS is not enough to
save you.  Learn to stop dying.

The remaining three (restful sleep, strangulation, change) are obviously
just rocks in the gumball machine, of course.  :)

